Roy L. Fuchs wrote:
> 
>  Whenever I try to sacrifice a large corpse it fails.  Does god only
> like small and medium sized corpses?

	Actually, as a very general rule, the gods like large corpses
better than small ones. They don't like old corpses, though, and large
ones are heavy and slow you down when you're dragging them around, so
you might just be having trouble getting them to the altar in time. (And
some of the biggest you won't be able to move at all, so if you want to
sacrifice them, you'd better kill them right on the altar. Or, well, the
gods don't mind if it's been chewed on a bit, so if you can arrange for
an interruption to your meal, you might be able to gnaw it down to
something you can lift...)

	Also note that undead corpses are always old, even if freshly
deprived of their unnatural unlife. Except, IIRC, wraiths. There are
usually better uses for wraith corpses, though.

